The woman types on her computer and registers me in the system.
She prints a paper and gives it to me.
"Here is your CPR number," she says.
It is a personal number, and you use it for everything in Denmark.
The number is important and very private.
I take good care of it and put the paper in my bag.
"Do you have a Danish phone number?" she asks.
"Yes, I have a new number," I answer.
I give her the number, and she notes it down.
Finally, she smiles warmly at me.
"Welcome to Denmark, Maya," she says.
"Thank you very much," I say happily.
